Title: **The Harbour Light**
Credit: A short scene for Fel's Voice Lab
Author: The Voice Lab tests
Draft date: 2026-11-12

# ACT ONE

= Mara waits for her brother at the lighthouse.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain against the glass. MARA (40s) trims the wick of a lantern.

[[The lamp should flicker here.]]

MARA
I kept the light on. *Every* night.

TOMAS (O.S.)
Mara? Is that you up there?

MARA
(calling down)
Who else would be fool enough to climb these stairs in this weather?

Tomas climbs into view, soaked.

TOMAS (CONT'D)
I came as soon as the boat was in.
(beat)
The harbour master says the storm turns at midnight.

/* An older draft had a long speech here.
TOMAS
Nobody will ever hear this.
*/

MARA
Then we wait.

TOMAS ^
Then we wait.

@McCLANE
(from the radio)
Lighthouse, this is the _Saint Brigid_. Do you read?

> The radio crackles. <

MARA (V.O.)
I read you, Saint Brigid. Keep to the light.

CUT TO:

===

EXT. HARBOUR WALL - LATER

The boat rounds the point, its lamps steady.

TOMAS
~Bring her home, bring her home.
